---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Data privacy">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">Data privacy</h1>
    <div class="mt-8 space-y-4 text-sm text-brand-gray">
      <p class="rounded-xl border border-dashed border-ink-600 bg-ink-900/60 p-5 text-brand-gray">
        Placeholder. Replace with a real privacy policy before this site is treated as production, covering at
        least: what this site collects (this build only pulls public data from the GitHub API at build time, and
        sets no cookies), what the mod and app collect once they exist, and how to request data deletion.
      </p>
      <div>
        <p class="font-semibold text-white">This site</p>
        <p>
          The landing site itself is static and sets no cookies or analytics. Contributor avatars and names shown
          on this site are pulled from GitHub's public API at build time.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-semibold text-white">The mod and app</p>
        <p>
          To be written once the pairing flow ships. In short: your Minecraft server keeps its own data; there is
          no third-party service collecting it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
